## Fix complete

**Root cause** (`src/import_merge.ts:7`): the duplicate check compared raw strings — `b.url === inc.url` — which is case-sensitive. Hostnames are case-insensitive, so `https://example.com/a` and `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` weren't recognized as the same URL, and the incoming bookmark was appended as a second entry.

**Change**: replaced the raw comparison with the repo's existing `normalizeUrl` helper (from `src/url_utils.ts`), which lowercases the hostname. This reuses existing, tested code rather than duplicating normalization.

**Verified**:
- `deno lint` and `deno check` both pass.
- Existing test suite still green (3 passed).
- Manual check: existing `https://example.com/a` + incoming `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` → 1 entry, tags unioned (`["x","y"]`), existing entry kept. A genuinely different URL (`https://other.com/a`) is still appended as a second entry.

One side note: `normalizeUrl` also strips tracking params and trailing slashes, so those now factor into dedup too. That matches how bookmark dedup is handled elsewhere in the repo, but flagging it in case you'd want hostname-only comparison.


